{"id": "sdqa0126", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.49, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1939, "eot_read_ms": 32, "reference_answer": "the process of encoding a message or information in such a way that only authorized parties can access it and those who are not authorized cannot", "query": "What is encryption?", "transcript": "What is encryption?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Encryption is the process of converting readable information, called plaintext, into an unreadable form, called ciphertext, using an algorithm and usually a key. Its purpose is to protect data so that only authorized people or systems with the correct key can read it.", "expert_answer": "Encryption is the process of converting readable information, called plaintext, into an unreadable form, called ciphertext, using an algorithm and usually a key. Its purpose is to protect data so that only authorized people or systems with the correct key can read it.\n\nExample: A message like “Hello” might be encrypted into something like “X7aQ9p,” which cannot be understood without decrypting it.", "expert_latency_s": 2.24, "stall_ms": 32, "relay_ms": 1770}
